Libsmb2 components fall under separate licences


The lib and include directories (except DCE/RPC)
===============================================
The smb2 client library itself, i.e. the lib directory and non-DCE/RPC
headers under include/, is licenced under GNU Lesser General Public
License as published by the Free Software Foundation; either version 2.1
of the License, or (at your option) any later version.

A copy of LGPL 2.1 is included in the file LICENCE-LGPL-2.1.txt but can
also be downloaded from
http://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/lgpl-2.1.html

This is the licence that applies to the libsmb2 library and its use.


The libdcerpc directory and DCE/RPC headers
===========================================
The DCE/RPC library (libdcerpc/) and the DCE/RPC public headers
(include/smb2/libsmb2-dcerpc*.h) are licenced under the 2-Clause BSD
License.

To avoid any confusion, every source file also contain a licence boilerplate.


The examples directory
======================
The example applications using this library, i.e. the examples directory,
is licenced under 2-Clause BSD License.

These are executable applications that link with the libsmb2 library
and/or libdcerpc.

To avoid any confusion, every source file also contain a licence boilerplate.
